  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "The evidence strongly identifies scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer + weighted as the optimal architecture (config_027: 0.725 acc), with imagenet_vit_l as the image encoder. The only remaining untested variable within this top-performing family is the image encoder: config_033 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + multiprofile + transformer + weighted) tests whether the smaller resnet50 backbone can match or approach vit_l's performance when paired with the superior scvi_n200 RNA encoder. From the scgpt comparisons (config_001 vs config_009), vit_l outperformed resnet50 by ~1.7%, but scvi_n200's stronger representations may interact differently with the image modality. This is the best use of the final experiment because: (1) it tests the one remaining design choice in the proven-best architecture, (2) if resnet50 matches vit_l, it offers a cheaper alternative for deployment, and (3) if it underperforms, it definitively confirms config_027 as the optimal configuration. Expected cost is moderate (~2.5–3.5 GPU hours), slightly cheaper than config_027 since resnet50 has fewer parameters than ViT-L, keeping total budget reasonable."
}

